{title: 422 - Marching to Zion}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #422 • MARCHING TO ZION • 12.16.12.12.15}
{lyricist: Isaac Watts}
{composer: Robert Lowry}
{key: F}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 422}
{meta: tune MARCHING TO ZION}
{meta: meter 12.16.12.12.15}
{meta: category Doctrines - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[F]Come ye that love the [C7]Lord, and let [F]your joys be known,
[F]Join in a song with [C]sweet accord, [Bb/F]Join in a song with [F]sweet accord.
[F/C]And thus [Gm]surround the throne, [C]and [F]thus surround [C]the throne.
[F]We&#39;re marching [Bb]to Zion, beautiful, [C7]beautiful [F]Zion;
[F]We&#39;re marching upward to Zion; the beautiful city of God
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Refrain}
[F]We're marching to [C]Zion,
[C]Beautiful, [F]beautiful [Bb]Zion;
[Bb]We're marching upward [F/C]to Zion,
[C7]The beautiful [F]city of God.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[F]Let those refuse to sing
[F]Who never [Bb/F]knew our [F]God;
[F/C]But [Gm]children of [C]the [F]heav'nly [C]King,
[F/C]But [Gm]children of [C]the [F]heav'nly [C]King
[F]May [Bb]speak their [F/C]joys [C7]abroad,
[F]May speak their joys abroad.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[F]The hill [C7]of [F]Zion yields
[F]A thousand [Bb]sacred [F]sweets
[F/C]Before [Gm]we reach [C]the [F]heav'nly [C]fields,
[F/C]Before [Gm]we reach [C]the [F]heav'nly [C]fields
[F]Or [Bb]walk the [F/C]golden streets,
[F]Or walk the golden streets.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[F]Then let our [C7]songs [F]abound
[F]And ev'ry [Bb/F]tear be [F]dry;
[F/C]We're [Gm]marching thru [C]Immanuel's ground,
[F/C]We're [Gm]marching thru [C]Immanuel's ground
[F]To [Bb]fairer [F/C]worlds [C7]on [F]high,
[F]To fairer worlds on high.
{end_of_verse}
